<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Qin (Xue Ju)</h1><p class="st-meta">617 CE – 618 CE · capital Tianshui</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived rebel empire in Gansu whose armies briefly beat the young Tang but were destroyed by Li Shimin in 618.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a>, a rich and powerful man of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanzhou">Jincheng</a> (modern Lanzhou), rose in revolt in 617 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sui-dynasty">Sui Dynasty</a> disintegrated. He took the title Hegemon-King of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-qin">Western Qin</a>, then proclaimed himself emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and moved his capital east to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianshui">Tianshui</a>, threatening the Wei valley around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime was essentially a military confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> frontier troops, known for their harsh treatment of captives, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a> appointed relatives and generals to the main offices rather than building a civil administration. Its aim was to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> itself. In 618 its army defeated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qianshuiyuan">Qianshuiyuan</a>, when Li Shimin was ill.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a> died soon after this victory, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-rengao">Xue Rengao</a> succeeded him. Later in 618 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> returned, wore down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> army and routed it at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qianshuiyuan">Qianshuiyuan</a>; Xue Rengao surrendered and was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, opening the north-west to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 617 CE – 618 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.98%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>617 CE – 618 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tianshui</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Xue Ju, Xue Rengao</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mahayana Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Western Qin (617-618)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=618&amp;focus=qin-xue-ju" aria-label="Qin (Xue Ju) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7296 876 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Qin (Xue Ju) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7616 1132L7769 1191M7616 1132L7771 1192"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7769 1191h0M7771 1192h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7616 1132h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7616 1132h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=618&amp;focus=qin-xue-ju">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
